# Module 11: Build Docker Images

Application:

```python
from flask import Flask

app = Flask(__name__)

@app.route("/")
def hello():
    return "Hello Docker"

app.run(host="0.0.0.0")
```

---

## Dockerfile

```dockerfile
FROM python:3.11

WORKDIR /app

COPY . .

RUN pip install flask

CMD ["python","app.py"]
```

Build:

```bash
docker build -t myapp:v1 .
```

Run:

```bash
docker run -p 5000:5000 myapp:v1
```

---

# Module 12: Docker Volumes

Problem:

Containers are temporary.

Delete container:

```bash
docker rm mysql
```

Data disappears.

---

Create Volume

```bash
docker volume create mysql-data
```

List Volumes:

```bash
docker volume ls
```

Run database:

```bash
docker run -d \
-v mysql-data:/var/lib/mysql \
mysql
```

Data survives container deletion.

---

# Module 13: Docker Networks

Create network:

```bash
docker network create app-net
```

List:

```bash
docker network ls
```

Run mysql:

```bash
docker run -d \
--network app-net \
--name mysql \
mysql
```

Run backend:

```bash
docker run -d \
--network app-net \
--name backend \
backend
```

Connect:

```text
mysql:3306
```

Container names become DNS records.

